5.1 Constructing Graphs
=======================

 -- Function: dag-draw-create-graph &optional attributes
     Create and return a new empty graph.  ATTRIBUTES is an optional
     hash table of graph-level attributes.

 -- Function: dag-draw-create-from-spec &rest spec
     Create a graph from a declarative specification and return it
     _unlaid-out_; call ‘dag-draw-layout-graph’ before rendering.  SPEC
     is a property list with two required keys:

     ‘:nodes’
          A list of node specifications.  Each is ‘(id :label "Label"
          ...attrs)’, where ID is a symbol and ‘:label’ is required.
          Remaining keyword properties become node attributes (see *note
          Node Attributes::).
     ‘:edges’
          A list of edge specifications.  Each is ‘(from to ...attrs)’,
          where FROM and TO are node ids.  Remaining keyword properties
          become edge attributes (see *note Edge Attributes::);
          ‘:weight’ and ‘:label’ are recognized specially.

     Signals an error if ‘:nodes’ or ‘:edges’ is missing, if a node
     lacks ‘:label’, if a node id is duplicated, or if an edge
     references an unknown node.

 -- Function: dag-draw-add-node graph node-id &optional label attributes
     Add a node to GRAPH and return the created node.  NODE-ID is a
     unique symbol.  LABEL is the display string (defaults to the symbol
     name).  ATTRIBUTES is an optional hash table of node attributes.
     The node is auto-sized to fit its label.

 -- Function: dag-draw-add-edge graph from-node to-node &optional weight
          label attributes
     Add an edge from FROM-NODE to TO-NODE in GRAPH and return it.
     WEIGHT defaults to ‘1’.  LABEL is an optional edge label.
     ATTRIBUTES is an optional hash table; a ‘min-length’ key sets the
     minimum rank span (default ‘1’).


File: dag-draw.info,  Node: Laying Out,  Next: Rendering,  Prev: Constructing Graphs,  Up: Reference

5.2 Laying Out
==============

 -- Function: dag-draw-layout-graph graph &rest args
     Run the GKNV layout algorithm on GRAPH in place and return it.
     This performs four passes: rank assignment, vertex ordering,
     coordinate positioning, and spline (edge route) generation.  ARGS
     accepts one keyword:

     ‘:coordinate-mode’
          ‘ascii’ (the default) produces compact integer coordinates
          suited to terminal output; ‘high-res’ is a legacy
          high-resolution mode.


File: dag-draw.info,  Node: Rendering,  Next: Querying,  Prev: Laying Out,  Up: Reference

5.3 Rendering
=============

 -- Function: dag-draw-render-graph graph &optional format selected
     Render a laid-out GRAPH and return a string.  FORMAT is one of:

     ‘ascii’
          Monospace Unicode box-drawing art.
     ‘svg’
          A complete SVG document.
     ‘dot’
          Graphviz DOT source.

     When FORMAT is omitted, ‘dag-draw-default-output-format’ is used.
     SELECTED is an optional node id to emphasize: a double-line box in
     ASCII, a glow filter in SVG, ‘style=bold’ in DOT.


File: dag-draw.info,  Node: Querying,  Next: Mutating,  Prev: Rendering,  Up: Reference

5.4 Querying
============

 -- Function: dag-draw-get-node graph node-id
     Return the node structure for NODE-ID, or ‘nil’.

 -- Function: dag-draw-graph-edges graph
     Return the list of all edge structures in GRAPH.

 -- Function: dag-draw-get-edges-from graph node-id
     Return the list of edges whose source is NODE-ID.

 -- Function: dag-draw-get-edges-to graph node-id
     Return the list of edges whose target is NODE-ID.

 -- Function: dag-draw-find-edge graph from-node to-node
     Return the edge from FROM-NODE to TO-NODE, or ‘nil’.

 -- Function: dag-draw-get-node-ids graph
     Return the list of all node ids.

 -- Function: dag-draw-node-count graph
     Return the number of nodes.

 -- Function: dag-draw-edge-count graph
     Return the number of edges.

 -- Function: dag-draw-get-successors graph node-id
     Return the list of node ids directly reachable from NODE-ID.

 -- Function: dag-draw-get-predecessors graph node-id
     Return the list of node ids that point directly to NODE-ID.

 -- Function: dag-draw-get-source-nodes graph
     Return the list of node ids that have no incoming edges.

 -- Function: dag-draw-get-graph-bounds graph
     Return ‘(min-x min-y max-x max-y)’, the bounding rectangle of the
     positioned graph.  Call after ‘dag-draw-layout-graph’.

 -- Function: dag-draw-detect-cycles graph
     Return the list of back-edges (edge structures) that close a cycle,
     or ‘nil’ if GRAPH is acyclic.  See *note Detecting Cycles::.


File: dag-draw.info,  Node: Mutating,  Next: Struct Accessors,  Prev: Querying,  Up: Reference

5.5 Mutating
============

 -- Function: dag-draw-remove-node graph node-id
     Remove the node NODE-ID from GRAPH.

 -- Function: dag-draw-remove-edge graph from-node to-node
